From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:47:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] EXA: no bilinear filtering of transformed repeating
 pictures

Broken: the texture unit does not wrap bilinear samples at the texture
edge, so a transformed RepeatNormal picture with the bilinear filter got
a visible seam every texture width.

Found: xformtest mismatches on the BM5 for transformed repeating
bilinear sources.

Fix: viaExaTransformOpSupported() rejects transformed repeating bilinear
pictures, so they go to software. Nearest-filtered repeats stay on the
3D engine.
---
 src/via_exa.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/via_exa.c b/src/via_exa.c
index 6e8d6b2..9f0045b 100644
--- a/src/via_exa.c
+++ b/src/via_exa.c
@@ -485,6 +485,12 @@ viaExaPictureSupported(PicturePtr pict, Bool allowTransform)
         if (pict->filter != PictFilterNearest &&
             pict->filter != PictFilterBilinear)
             return FALSE;
+        /*
+         * Bilinear filtering doesn't wrap at the texture edge: a repeating
+         * picture got a visible seam every texture width.
+         */
+        if (pict->repeat && pict->filter == PictFilterBilinear)
+            return FALSE;
         if (d->width > 2048 || d->height > 2048)
             return FALSE;
         /*
